<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.8"/>
    <code code="51848-0" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation note"/>
    <title>Assessment</title>
    <text><list><item>Postmenopausal bleeding for three weeks, about eight years after her last period, in a woman of 60 who takes no hormone therapy: endometrial cancer must be excluded. Office endometrial biopsy taken today, transvaginal ultrasound this week, and gynecologic oncology review booked: active, confirmed [S]</item></list></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.10" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="18776-5" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Plan of care note"/>
    <title>Plan of Treatment</title>
    <text><list><item>Any bleeding after menopause is evaluated: speculum and bimanual examination, office endometrial biopsy at the first visit, and transvaginal ultrasound within the week, both done rather than relying on endometrial thickness alone; blood count and A1c; results by telephone within days, not at a routine visit. Guideline: Updated Guidance Regarding the Role of Transvaginal Ultrasonography in Evaluating the Endometrium of Individuals With Postmenopausal Bleeding. Obstet Gynecol 2026;148(1):e87-e91 (PMID 41990335) (2026); Committee Opinion No. 734: The Role of Transvaginal Ultrasonography in Evaluating the Endometrium of Women With Postmenopausal Bleeding. Obstet Gynecol 2018;131(5):e124-e129 (PMID 29683909) (2018); Clarke MA, et al. Racial and Ethnic Differences in Hysterectomy-Corrected Uterine Corpus Cancer Mortality by Stage and Histologic Subtype. JAMA Oncol 2022;8(6):895-903 (PMID 35511145) (2022); Doll KM, et al. Assessment of Prediagnostic Experiences of Black Women With Endometrial Cancer in the United States. JAMA Netw Open 2020;3(5):e204954 (PMID 32412636) (2020) [S]</item><item>Distress and depression screening at each visit, plain explanations, written information, and support she chooses; she decides who receives each note. Guideline: NCCN Clinical Practice Guidelines in Oncology: Uterine Neoplasms (2026); Depression and Suicide Risk in Adults: Screening (2023) [S]</item><item ID="referral-order">Referral to gynecologic oncology, Miriam Delacroix, MD, ordered 2026-01-05 [S]</item></list></text>

